cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this candidate, its ephemeris or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "TIC 38699429.01: independent detection and vetting of a 2.7 Earth-radius, 11.72-day transit candidate in the conservative habitable zone of the M dwarf TIC 38699429"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Paliwal
    given-names: Advait
    email: advaitpaliwal@gmail.com
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC38699429"
url: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC38699429"
abstract: >-
  Independent detection and vetting of a transit signal on TIC 38699429, an M
  dwarf (Teff 2914 K, 0.166 solar radii) at 57.5 pc in the TESS southern
  continuous viewing zone. The signal was first posted publicly by Benoit
  (2026, Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23598218) and also by Reckling (2026,
  Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23635149); this record makes no claim of first
  detection. TESS-SPOC photometry from 31 sectors (2018 to 2023) shows 60
  transits. Period 11.718167 +/- 0.000013 d, mid-transit BJD_TDB 2459196.67148
  +/- 0.00072, depth 22,130 +/- 750 ppm, duration 1.47 h, radius 2.72 +/- 0.13
  Earth radii, insolation 0.66 +/- 0.15 times Earth's, inside the conservative
  habitable zone (Kopparapu et al. 2013). Difference images rule out the 25 Gaia
  stars within 150 arcsec brighter than G = 20.5. TRICERATOPS false-positive
  probability 0.064 with no neighbours removed and 0.026 with the
  pixel-excluded neighbours removed. A planet candidate, not a validated or
  confirmed planet.
keywords:
  - exoplanet
  - transit
  - TESS
  - planet candidate
  - habitable zone
  - M dwarf
  - TIC 38699429
